      <title>Critical mineral mining faces risks if local communities aren’t consulted enough: Case of lithium in Ghana</title>
      <link>https://www.downtoearth.org.in/africa/critical-mineral-mining-faces-risks-if-local-communities-arent-consulted-enough-case-of-lithium-in-ghana</link>
      <description>Mining critical minerals like lithium in Ghana faces risks if local communities are excluded from decision-making, leading to social conflicts and project delays. Effective risk management requires community engagement to ensure social legitimacy and stable supply chains for the energy transition.</description>
